# HTTP API Documentation

Any exposed HTTP endpoint MUST be documented so other clients and agents can integrate without reading source code.

## Location

- Index: `docs/api/README.md`
- Per-area or versioned detail: `docs/api/<resource>.md` (e.g. `items.md`, `reminders.md`)

Update the index when adding a new resource doc.

## When to Document

Document when you add or change:

- Route path, method, or handler behavior
- Request or response shape
- Status codes or error payloads
- Auth requirements or headers

## Entry Template

Use this structure for each endpoint in the resource doc:

```markdown
### `POST /api/v1/items`

Create a tend item.

**Auth:** Bearer token (required)

**Request body**
| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| title | string | yes | Display name |
| type | `"must"` \| `"want"` | yes | Reminder strictness |

**Responses**
| Status | Body | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| 201 | `Item` | Created |
| 400 | `{ error: string }` | Validation failure |
| 401 | `{ error: string }` | Missing or invalid auth |

**Example**
\`\`\`json
{ "title": "Water plants", "type": "want", "rhythmDays": 3 }
\`\`\`
```

## Keep Docs in Sync

API docs are part of the change — update them in the same PR/commit as the endpoint, not later.
